# GitHub attaches auto-generated "Source code (zip)" and "Source code (tar.gz)"
# archives to every release. There is no setting to hide those links, but the
# archives are produced with `git archive`, which honors `export-ignore`.
#
# This repository publishes only public release builds (attached as Release
# assets) and the metadata other sites read. It must never ship source code, so
# every tracked file is excluded from the generated archives, leaving them empty.
#
# Note: this only affects tags created after this file is committed; re-tag an
# existing release if you need its archive emptied too.
* export-ignore
